INCIDENTAL FIX (pre-existing, build-blocking; in allowed scope)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Localizable.xcstrings had 5 DEAD (zero references) plural-noun keys
(translation.bulk.itemDefault / .noun.rule / .noun.notification / .noun.session /
 .noun.drive) whose plural variations did not reference the number. Xcode 26's
xcstringstool rejects this ("Plural variation requires referencing the number"),
which fails ANY real catalog compile. The watch build is the first xcodebuild on
this host to actually compile the catalog (iOS/macOS were KMP-deferred), so it
surfaced the latent error. Fixed per Apple guidance by referencing the count
(%lld) in each plural value (30 values). Zero behavioural impact (unused keys);
unblocks every Apple target's catalog compile.

